WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.003
Imagine a stove that cooks your food

2
00:00:02.003 --> 00:00:04.395
and leaves you with more firewood than

3
00:00:04.395 --> 00:00:05.939
you started with.

4
00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:08.305
That's the idea of a breeder reactor.

5
00:00:08.705 --> 00:00:09.390
In its core,

6
00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:13.233
plutonium splits and throws out fast neutrons.

7
00:00:13.233 --> 00:00:16.077
Some hit ordinary uranium-238 placed around the

8
00:00:16.077 --> 00:00:18.492
core, and turn it into new plutonium.

9
00:00:18.492 --> 00:00:20.058
Fuel is bred.

10
00:00:20.458 --> 00:00:23.291
Ordinary reactors slow their neutrons with water.

11
00:00:23.291 --> 00:00:24.649
A breeder keeps them fast,

12
00:00:24.649 --> 00:00:27.018
so it is cooled by liquid sodium

13
00:00:27.018 --> 00:00:28.374
metal instead.

14
00:00:28.774 --> 00:00:31.282
India's Prototype Fast Breeder Reactor,

15
00:00:31.282 --> 00:00:33.255
five hundred megawatts,

16
00:00:33.255 --> 00:00:36.158
is at Kalpakkam in Tamil Nadu.

17
00:00:36.158 --> 00:00:37.992
Loading of its core began in March

18
00:00:37.992 --> 00:00:39.430
twenty twenty-four.

19
00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:41.827
India has little uranium but a great

20
00:00:41.827 --> 00:00:43.267
deal of thorium.

21
00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:44.706
Breeders build up the fuel and,

22
00:00:44.706 --> 00:00:48.814
later, can turn thorium into usable uranium-233.

23
00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:50.063
It isn't easy.

24
00:00:50.063 --> 00:00:52.013
Sodium catches fire in air and reacts

25
00:00:52.013 --> 00:00:54.939
with water, so the engineering is demanding

26
00:00:54.939 --> 00:00:57.131
and the build has taken many years.

27
00:00:57.531 --> 00:00:58.564
For GS Three:

28
00:00:58.564 --> 00:01:00.143
a fast breeder makes more fuel than

29
00:01:00.143 --> 00:01:02.361
it burns, and it is stage two

30
00:01:02.361 --> 00:01:04.751
of India's three-stage nuclear plan.

